# The fusion side of `F Phi`, where the model has arranged for there to be nothing. One row per
# composition: the fusions it declares, how many of them are a row of the matrix, the rank that
# follows, and the dimension of the left null space.
#
# Two subspaces, and one number decides both
#   The rows of `F Phi` have disjoint supports and none of them is zero, so they are independent
#   and the rank is simply how many rows there are. The column space is then the whole of the
#   space the declared fusions span exactly when every declared fusion IS a row, and the left null
#   space is the rest. So `rank` and `left_null` are not two measurements, they are one count read
#   from each end, and `declared = rank + left_null` is the statement that they partition.
#   Proof: `src/proofs/README.md`, entry `fold_subspaces`.
#
# What a non-zero left null space would mean
#   A vector in it is a combination of composed figures that no assignment to the parts can
#   produce. In this model that is not a subtle condition: it is a declared fusion with no column
#   under it at all, so its figure is owed by a sum over an empty set. `asrt:Fusion/part` is
#   `minOccurs="1"`, so the filing cannot say it directly, and the state is reached the other way,
#   through a part whose filing this corpus does not hold.
#
# Which is why the count here is of RESOLVED parts and the other law's is not
#   `algebra/fusions_have_parts.sqlc` drives from the references a composer FILED, and it is right
#   to: whether a fusion named a part is a question about the document, and the answer does not
#   depend on what else was loaded. This relation asks the matrix's question instead, and a
#   reference to a filing nobody has is no column. So the two can part company, and the set where
#   they do is `composition/unresolved_parts.sqlc`. Neither is the other's check.
#
# Refused rather than corrected, which is the same shape as the cycle space
#   `checks/unresolved_part.sqlc` accuses a part that does not resolve, so a conforming corpus has
#   no such part and this dimension is zero in every conforming document. That is not the
#   arithmetic coming out flat, it is a rule holding it there, and the layer graph's cycle space
#   is zero for exactly the same kind of reason. Both are laws that would have something to report
#   if a rule were removed.
#
# Per composition, because that is who is answerable
#   A composition is one filer's claim, so a fusion missing its columns is that filer's document
#   to repair even when the missing filing is somebody else's. Reporting one number for the corpus
#   would name nobody.
#
# Probe
#   `algebra/composition_image.sqlc` holds `left_null = 0` with the declared count as its floor.
#   In a rolled-back transaction, delete the layer a part names and this relation must show one
#   dimension on that composition and nowhere else.
-- composition/fusions.sqlc against the fusions that are a row of F Phi.
SELECT f.filing                                         AS composition,
       count(*)                                         AS declared,
       count(k.composition)                             AS rank,
       count(*) - count(k.composition)                  AS left_null
FROM      (
    :compose(composition/fusions.sqlc)
) f
LEFT JOIN (
    :compose(rank/composition_kernel.sqlc)
) k ON k.composition = f.filing AND k.composed_layer = f.layer
GROUP BY f.filing
